aarch64 #11 Tier 1: cache the mach_task_self() legacy function to skip a per-call RPC.

DSERVER_TRACE_CALLS shows ~6.7 task_self_trap RPCs per spawned process. mach_task_self() has a cached
form (the mach_init.h macro -> mach_task_self_, set once at init) but the mach_legacy.c FUNCTION calls
task_self_trap() every time, so cross-dylib callers that reach the function symbol pay an RPC per call.
The task self port is a fork-stable well-known port (the macro already relies on that across fork) and
is not a caller-deallocated ref (unlike mach_host_self/mach_thread_self), so return the cached global.
---
--- a/libsyscall/mach/mach_legacy.c
+++ b/libsyscall/mach/mach_legacy.c
@@ -41,7 +41,12 @@
 mach_port_t
 mach_task_self(void)
 {
-	return task_self_trap();
+	// aarch64 #11 Tier 1: task self is a fork-stable well-known port, already fetched once into
+	// mach_task_self_ at mach_init and used by the mach_task_self() MACRO everywhere. Cross-dylib
+	// callers of this FUNCTION otherwise dserver_rpc_task_self_trap on every call (~6.7 RPC/spawn).
+	// Return the cached global (it is not a deallocated ref, unlike host/thread self), falling back
+	// to the trap only before mach_init has set it.
+	return (mach_task_self_ != MACH_PORT_NULL) ? mach_task_self_ : task_self_trap();
 }
 
 mach_port_t
